var body: some View { Page("Badge", description: "A short label that names a state or a count. It is not interactive, so it wears only the resting state of a control recipe and deliberately skips the shared state machine — a label that changed colour under the pointer would read as something you can press. Pick the recipe with `variant`, pick the ramp it resolves against with `tint`.") { Section("Variant and tint", description: "Every combination the two axes allow — three of the six recipes, the ones that read as a label rather than as a control — plus the one variant the badge owns. `raised` is paper fill and quiet ink, no ramp: the chip that sits on a grey card, where a `tinted` neutral would sink into the card and a `filled` one would shout. There is no `normal` or `plain` badge, because both would be text with padding around it.") { Stack { Specimen("filled") { Badge(size: .medium, variant: .filled, tint: .primary) { HStack(spacing: 0) { Text("Primary") } }
